{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), evidence is extremely sparse. The most fundamental uncertainty is whether the image modality carries any predictive signal at all. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean, single-variable comparison with config_001 that isolates the modality effect while keeping profile setting (singleprofile) and model simplicity (no aggregation, no fusion) constant. This is the highest-information next step: if image-only performs comparably or better than RNA-only, it validates pursuing multimodal fusion (configs 016–051); if it performs poorly, it redirects budget toward improving the RNA side (encoder, multiprofile). Without this baseline, any multimodal result would be uninterpretable because we could not attribute performance to fusion quality versus the strength of the individual modalities. It is the best use of one experiment to reduce uncertainty about the most consequential design axis."
}

